@1 = ~Aye, ye know what? I'm thinkin' I recognise this bloom. It's the Mourning Lace flower, straight out o' the Durpar kingdom. They grow in absolute blackness, mind ye, as the sun completely blocks their ability to sprout.~
@2 = ~They bring on fierce hallucinations and that sleep paralysis phenomenon. Ye cannae smell 'em from afar, but just standin' too close to the blasted things will give ye the very same visions. I don'na think we'll be needin' any exorcisms here. There ain't no foul spirits at play. The effects o' this flower will pass right away, just as soon as it's tossed out o' the building.~
@3 = ~I am unfamiliar with this particular flower, jaluk — but it mimics the absolute dark of the Underdark beautifully. Its venom forces the mind to weave its own suffocating nightmares, a lesson your fragile surface-dwellers sorely need. Do not waste my time chanting foolish exorcisms; there is no spirit here to banish. Toss the weed into the sun, let the light wither it.~
@4 = ~By Valkur's blade. <CHARNAME>, look at this. The Mourning Lace flower. It weaves a cruel illusion in the mind of any who breathe its scent. The coward's poison is weak, masking itself until standing directly over it. We must inform Allesia. Once she purges this vile weed from the hall, the children will be safe.~
@5 = ~(Strange feeling overcomes you when you approach the flower. Its scent is sweet, honey-like yet amplified with a chilling sensation of something quite off. Its odour is delicate, but it sharpens your senses. You begin to feel slightly nauseous and your skin generated goosebumps.)~
@6 = ~Yeslick? What is this?~
@7 = ~Viconia. That flower...~
@8 = ~Branwen? Something stands out about this flower.~
@9 = ~Leave.~
